# ============================================================================
# Bethesda SMS — environment configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself.
# ============================================================================

# --- Database (required) ---------------------------------------------------
# Postgres connection string. Any managed Postgres works (Supabase, Neon,
# Railway, RDS, a local instance) — Prisma 7 talks to it via @prisma/adapter-pg,
# not a bundled query engine, so this is the only DB-related variable needed.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/bethesda_sms"

# --- Better Auth (required) -------------------------------------------------
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET encrypts session tokens — generate a long random string,
# e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. Rotating it invalidates all active sessions.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="generate-a-long-random-string"
# Must match the URL the app is actually served from (used to set the
# session cookie's domain/secure flags correctly). Update for production.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Attendance device sync bridge (required if using the ZKTeco device) ---
# Shared secret between this app and sync-bridge/ (the Raspberry Pi script
# that polls the ZKTeco K40 fingerprint unit and pushes logs to
# /api/attendance/sync). Must be identical in both .env files. If your
# location has no biometric device, staff can still sign in/out from
# /attendance/sign (source: WEB_SELF) and you can leave this as a random
# placeholder — it just won't be exercised.
DEVICE_SYNC_SECRET="generate-a-long-random-string"

# --- Email notifications (strongly recommended — see note below) ----------
# Powers src/lib/notifications.ts: late check-in alerts to supervisors,
# leave-decision emails to staff, AND password-reset OTP codes (forgot
# password flow at /forgot-password). Get a key at https://resend.com —
# the free tier covers a school/NGO's volume comfortably.
#
# Leaving this blank does NOT break the app for attendance/leave/staff —
# those notifications just no-op with a console warning. But it DOES
# effectively disable self-service password reset: in development the OTP
# code is logged to the server console as a fallback so the flow is still
# testable, but in production the OTP is never logged anywhere (logs are
# typically less access-controlled than email), so a locked-out admin
# would have no way to receive their code. Set this before going live.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# --- SMS notifications (optional, NOT YET WIRED UP) -------------------------
# Reserved for a future SMS channel (e.g. late check-in texts to staff
# without email access) via Termii (https://termii.com — popular for
# Nigerian phone numbers, unlike Twilio which is pricier for NGN routes).
# No code currently reads this variable — it's a placeholder for that work.
# Leave blank; do not treat this as "already working" until it's implemented.
TERMII_API_KEY=""

# --- Third-party integrations NOT included in this build --------------------
# Deliberately left out of this pass — the Visitors and Donations modules
# are manual record-books (front desk / finance staff type entries in),
# not payment or check-in integrations. If you want these later, they'd be
# separate services with their own env vars, e.g.:
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=""   # online giving form -> webhook creates Donation rows
#   FLUTTERWAVE_SECRET_KEY="" # alternative to Paystack for NGN online payments
# Neither is required for the app to run — donations are logged manually by
# HR/Admin from the Donations page regardless of whether either is added.
